<title>BELGIUM: ERM bilateral central rates of markka vs others.</title>
<headline>ERM bilateral central rates of markka vs others.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The EU monetary committee agreed the central rate for the Finnish markka, which joined the Exchange Rate Mechanism on Saturday, should be 5.80661 for one European Currency Unit (Ecu).</p>
<p>The bilateral central rates of the markka against the other currencies of the exchange-rate mechanism, rounded to six significant figures, will be for 100 markka as follows:</p>
<p>    Belgian franc	 678.468</p>
<p>    Danish krone	  125.474</p>
<p>    German mark	    32.8948</p>
<p>    Spanish peseta     2798.41</p>
<p>    French franc	  110.324</p>
<p>    Irish pound	    13.6433</p>
<p>    Luxembourg franc    678.468</p>
<p>    Dutch guilder	  37.0636</p>
<p>    Austrian schilling  231.431</p>
<p>    Portuguese escudo  3371.88</p>
<p>The current fluctuation margins of 15 percent will be observed around these bilateral rates. All other bilateral central rates and intervention rates within the exchange rate mechanism remain unchanged.</p>
</text>
